login to the ubuntu instance, make a folder 
$ mkdir (project)
$ wget (https://docs.docker.com/reference/dockerfile) application link
install unzip and unzip the file
$ sudo apt install unzip -y
$ unzip (filename)
cd into the unzip folder and tar the files because we cannot extract the zip folder in image
$ cd (filename)
$ tar czvf (build_image).tar.gz * # this command will tar the files to a .tar folder
$ mv (build_image).tar.gz ../       # this command moves the folder to one level up
remove the zip and unzip files as we have the tar file
now move the build_image to project
$ mv (build_image).tar.gz project/
inside prokect folder write the Dockerfile
$ vim DockerFile (see the dockerfile and edit it)
after completion of Dockerfile build the image
$ docker build -t (build_image)img .    # in place of . we need to give the path if the file is in other location
now test the image by building a container using the image
$ docker run -d --name (mywebsite) -p 9080:80 (build_image)img 
after the container created, test the application by taking public ip and port (19.173.153.75:9080) this ip should be working in chrome.

now we can push this image to publish in docker hub
create an accont in docker hub
$ docker login (give the username and password)
to push the image the image name should be (username)/(build_image)img (just build the image like this)
$ docker push (username)/(build_image)img  (this command will push the image)
we can check the image in docker hub

